IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei2-nouns`
IMPORT `ei2-seat`

-- Worked cases for ei2-seat (Employment Insurance Act, ss 23.3(6) to 65.2): one or more per question, in the facts a person in the
-- seat would state. Expected values are written by hand from the text of the Act, before running. A name is a person in the example;
-- a comment says which words of the Act give the answer. Several cases sit either side of each threshold, date and figure.


§ `Mei cares for her father, a critically ill adult (s 23.3(6) to (9))`

-- Q1. Mei and her brother Kai both claim; 20 weeks remain: only 15 may be divided (s 23.3(6): "up to a maximum of 15 weeks")
#ASSERT `How many of the remaining weeks can we divide between us` TRUE TRUE 20 EQUALS 15
-- Q1. 10 weeks remain: all 10 may be divided
#ASSERT `How many of the remaining weeks can we divide between us` TRUE TRUE 10 EQUALS 10
-- Q1. Kai has not claimed: nothing may be divided under the subsection
#ASSERT `How many of the remaining weeks can we divide between us` TRUE FALSE 10 EQUALS 0
-- Q1. Mei has not claimed under s 23.3
#ASSERT `How many of the remaining weeks can we divide between us` FALSE TRUE 10 EQUALS 0
-- Q2. Mei and Kai agreed how to divide the weeks: the prescribed rules do not decide it (s 23.3(6) first sentence)
#ASSERT NOT `Do the prescribed rules decide how the weeks are divided` TRUE
-- Q2. they cannot agree: the prescribed rules divide the weeks (s 23.3(6) second sentence)
#ASSERT `Do the prescribed rules decide how the weeks are divided` FALSE
-- Q3. Together they would divide 16 weeks: over the 15-week ceiling (s 23.3(7))
#ASSERT `Would dividing this many weeks go over the ceiling` TRUE TRUE 16
-- Q3. 15 weeks is not over the ceiling
#ASSERT NOT `Would dividing this many weeks go over the ceiling` TRUE TRUE 15
-- Q3. Kai is not claiming under s 152.062: s 23.3(7) is not engaged
#ASSERT NOT `Would dividing this many weeks go over the ceiling` TRUE FALSE 16
-- Q4. Mei claims compassionate care benefits for the week of Sunday 1 March 2026; the adult's period runs 1 March to 29 August 2026 (s 23.3(8))
#ASSERT `Are compassionate care benefits unpayable to me this week` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 8 29)
-- Q4. the week of Sunday 30 August 2026 is after the period
#ASSERT NOT `Are compassionate care benefits unpayable to me this week` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 8 30) (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 8 29)
-- Q4. Mei claims a benefit that is not compassionate care
#ASSERT NOT `Are compassionate care benefits unpayable to me this week` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 8 29)
-- Q5. benefits are payable to Mei and a provincial plan pays for the same reasons (s 23.3(9))
#ASSERT `Will my benefits be reduced or eliminated because of a provincial law` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Q5. the provincial payments are for other reasons
#ASSERT NOT `Will my benefits be reduced or eliminated because of a provincial law` TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `Work-sharing, courses and employment support measures (ss 24 to 26)`

-- Q6. Dev works in work-sharing employment this week (s 24(3))
#ASSERT `Does section 24(3) treat me as unemployed and available this week` TRUE
-- Q6. a week without work-sharing employment: s 24(3) does not apply
#ASSERT NOT `Does section 24(3) treat me as unemployed and available this week` FALSE
-- Q7. the Commission's direction disapproving Dev's employer's work-sharing agreement is closed to review (s 24(2))
#ASSERT `Is the direction on a work-sharing agreement closed to review` TRUE
-- Q7. some other decision: s 24(2) does not close it
#ASSERT NOT `Is the direction on a work-sharing agreement closed to review` FALSE
-- Q8. Dev attends a course at his own expense, referred by the Commission (s 25(1)(a))
#ASSERT `Does section 25(1)(a) treat me as unemployed and available during my course` TRUE TRUE FALSE `ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training` FALSE TRUE
-- Q8. he enrolled without a referral
#ASSERT NOT `Does section 25(1)(a) treat me as unemployed and available during my course` TRUE TRUE FALSE `ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training` FALSE FALSE
-- Q8. the course is under an s 59(a) measure and the Commission referred him (not at own expense)
#ASSERT `Does section 25(1)(a) treat me as unemployed and available during my course` TRUE FALSE TRUE `ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training` FALSE TRUE
-- Q8. the course is under an s 59(b) measure only
#ASSERT NOT `Does section 25(1)(a) treat me as unemployed and available during my course` TRUE FALSE TRUE `ei2 s 59(b) measure providing employment opportunities or employment support` FALSE TRUE
-- Q8. the course is under a measure that is the subject of an s 63 agreement
#ASSERT `Does section 25(1)(a) treat me as unemployed and available during my course` TRUE FALSE FALSE `ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training` TRUE TRUE
-- Q9. Dev takes part in an activity assisted under an s 59(b) measure that the Regulations prescribe, referred (s 25(1)(b))
#ASSERT `Does section 25(1)(b) treat me as unemployed and available during my activity` TRUE TRUE `ei2 s 59(b) measure providing employment opportunities or employment support` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Q9. the measure is an s 59(c) measure (excluded by s 25(1)(b)(i))
#ASSERT NOT `Does section 25(1)(b) treat me as unemployed and available during my activity` TRUE TRUE `ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Q9. the measure is not prescribed
#ASSERT NOT `Does section 25(1)(b) treat me as unemployed and available during my activity` TRUE TRUE `ei2 s 59(b) measure providing employment opportunities or employment support` FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Q9. assistance under a prescribed measure that is the subject of an s 63 agreement
#ASSERT `Does section 25(1)(b) treat me as unemployed and available during my activity` TRUE FALSE `ei2 s 59(b) measure providing employment opportunities or employment support` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Q10. the Commission's decision on Dev's referral is closed to review (s 25(2))
#ASSERT `Is the decision about my referral closed to review` TRUE
-- Q10. some other decision
#ASSERT NOT `Is the decision about my referral closed to review` FALSE
-- Q11. benefits paid while Dev is employed under an s 59(b) measure are not earnings (s 26)
#ASSERT `Does section 26 say my benefits are not earnings` TRUE TRUE `ei2 s 59(b) measure providing employment opportunities or employment support` FALSE
-- Q11. an s 59(c) measure is excluded and there is no s 63 agreement
#ASSERT NOT `Does section 26 say my benefits are not earnings` TRUE TRUE `ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services` FALSE
-- Q11. an s 59(c) measure but the employment is also under an s 63 agreement measure
#ASSERT `Does section 26 say my benefits are not earnings` TRUE TRUE `ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services` TRUE
-- Q11. no benefits are paid while so employed
#ASSERT NOT `Does section 26 say my benefits are not earnings` FALSE TRUE `ei2 s 59(b) measure providing employment opportunities or employment support` FALSE

§ `Priya, who has not been looking for work, and Raj, whose referral ended (ss 27 and 28)`

-- Q12. Priya has not applied for a suitable vacancy, without good cause (s 27(1)(a))
#ASSERT `Am I disqualified because of what I did or did not do since my interruption of earnings` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Q12. she has good cause for what she did
#ASSERT NOT `Am I disqualified because of what I did or did not do since my interruption of earnings` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Q12. the Commission's direction to her was not reasonable (s 27(1)(c))
#ASSERT NOT `Am I disqualified because of what I did or did not do since my interruption of earnings` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Q12. she did not attend an interview the Commission directed to give her information (s 27(1)(d)(i))
#ASSERT `Am I disqualified because of what I did or did not do since my interruption of earnings` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Q12. she did nothing wrong
#ASSERT NOT `Am I disqualified because of what I did or did not do since my interruption of earnings` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Q13. Raj was expelled from a course assisted under an s 59(b) measure; the Commission ended the referral (s 27(1.1))
#ASSERT `Am I disqualified because my referral to a course, program or activity ended` TRUE TRUE `ei2 s 59(b) measure providing employment opportunities or employment support` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Q13. Raj did not attend without good cause and the Commission thinks he is unlikely to complete it
#ASSERT `Am I disqualified because my referral to a course, program or activity ended` TRUE TRUE `ei2 s 59(b) measure providing employment opportunities or employment support` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Q13. he did not attend, but the Commission does not think he is unlikely to complete it
#ASSERT NOT `Am I disqualified because my referral to a course, program or activity ended` TRUE TRUE `ei2 s 59(b) measure providing employment opportunities or employment support` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Q13. the measure is an s 59(c) measure
#ASSERT NOT `Am I disqualified because my referral to a course, program or activity ended` TRUE TRUE `ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Q13. the Commission did not end the referral
#ASSERT NOT `Am I disqualified because my referral to a course, program or activity ended` TRUE TRUE `ei2 s 59(b) measure providing employment opportunities or employment support` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Q14. ground (a): the Act says not fewer than 7 weeks (s 28(1)(a))
#ASSERT `What is the fewest weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1)(a) not applying for, or not accepting, a suitable employment` EQUALS JUST 7
-- Q14. ground (c): no least number is stated
#ASSERT `What is the fewest weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Q14. ground (1.1): no least number is stated
#ASSERT `What is the fewest weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1.1) referral to a course, program or activity terminated` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Q14. ground (d): no least number is stated
#ASSERT `What is the fewest weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1)(d) not attending an interview directed by the Commission` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Q14. ground (b): not fewer than 7
#ASSERT `What is the fewest weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1)(b) not taking advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment` EQUALS JUST 7
-- Q15. ground (a): the Act sets a least number of weeks
#ASSERT `Does section 28(1) set a least number of weeks for my ground` `ei2 s 27(1)(a) not applying for, or not accepting, a suitable employment`
-- Q15. ground (b)
#ASSERT `Does section 28(1) set a least number of weeks for my ground` `ei2 s 27(1)(b) not taking advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment`
-- Q15. ground (c): no least number
#ASSERT NOT `Does section 28(1) set a least number of weeks for my ground` `ei2 s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission`
-- Q15. ground (d): no least number
#ASSERT NOT `Does section 28(1) set a least number of weeks for my ground` `ei2 s 27(1)(d) not attending an interview directed by the Commission`
-- Q15. ground (1.1): no least number
#ASSERT NOT `Does section 28(1) set a least number of weeks for my ground` `ei2 s 27(1.1) referral to a course, program or activity terminated`
-- Q16. ground (a): not more than 12
#ASSERT `What is the most weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1)(a) not applying for, or not accepting, a suitable employment` EQUALS 12
-- Q16. ground (1.1): not more than 6
#ASSERT `What is the most weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1.1) referral to a course, program or activity terminated` EQUALS 6
-- Q16. ground (d): not more than 6
#ASSERT `What is the most weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1)(d) not attending an interview directed by the Commission` EQUALS 6
-- Q17. Priya's ground is (a) and the Commission set 7 weeks
#ASSERT `Is the number of weeks the Commission set within what the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1)(a) not applying for, or not accepting, a suitable employment` 7
-- Q17. the Commission set 13 weeks for ground (a)
#ASSERT NOT `Is the number of weeks the Commission set within what the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1)(a) not applying for, or not accepting, a suitable employment` 13
-- Q17. ground (c): 6 weeks
#ASSERT `Is the number of weeks the Commission set within what the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission` 6
-- Q17. ground (c): 7 weeks
#ASSERT NOT `Is the number of weeks the Commission set within what the Act allows` `ei2 s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission` 7
-- Q18. 5 weeks of disqualification; this is the 3rd week after the waiting period; she is not otherwise entitled to benefits (s 28(2))
#ASSERT `Is this week one I must serve as a week of disqualification` 5 3 FALSE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)` FALSE
-- Q18. this is the 6th week of 5
#ASSERT NOT `Is this week one I must serve as a week of disqualification` 5 6 FALSE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)` FALSE
-- Q18. she is otherwise entitled to maternity benefits this week: special benefits, so the serving is deferred (s 28(5))
#ASSERT NOT `Is this week one I must serve as a week of disqualification` 5 3 TRUE `pregnancy` FALSE
-- Q18. she is otherwise entitled only to regular benefits: not special benefits, so no deferral
#ASSERT `Is this week one I must serve as a week of disqualification` 5 3 TRUE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)` FALSE
-- Q18. otherwise entitled to benefits under s 25: deferred
#ASSERT NOT `Is this week one I must serve as a week of disqualification` 5 3 FALSE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)` TRUE
-- Q19. 4 weeks unserved; a later benefit period starts 5 January 2026, within two years of the event on 15 March 2025; 699 hours (s 28(3), (4))
#ASSERT `How many weeks of my disqualification carry forward` 4 (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2026 1 5) 699 EQUALS 4
-- Q19. 700 hours since the event: nothing carries forward (s 28(4))
#ASSERT `How many weeks of my disqualification carry forward` 4 (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2026 1 5) 700 EQUALS 0
-- Q19. the later benefit period starts more than two years after
#ASSERT `How many weeks of my disqualification carry forward` 4 (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2027 3 16) 0 EQUALS 0
-- Q20. benefits are deemed paid for a week of disqualification (s 28(6))
#ASSERT `Are benefits treated as paid to me for this week of disqualification` TRUE
-- Q20. not a week of disqualification
#ASSERT NOT `Are benefits treated as paid to me for this week of disqualification` FALSE
-- Q21. a minor attachment claimant asks to cancel and have a major attachment benefit period for special benefits (s 28(7))
#ASSERT `Can I still make the request despite the deeming of benefits as paid` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Q21. she does not want special benefits
#ASSERT NOT `Can I still make the request despite the deeming of benefits as paid` TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `Losing or leaving a job (ss 29 to 35)`

-- Q22. the employment is within her qualifying period (s 29(a))
#ASSERT `Is this employment one that counts under sections 30 to 33` TRUE FALSE
-- Q22. within neither period
#ASSERT NOT `Is this employment one that counts under sections 30 to 33` FALSE FALSE
-- Q23. Ana was dismissed (s 29(b))
#ASSERT `Does the Act count what happened as the loss of my employment` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Q23. she was dismissed for union activity: not a loss of employment for ss 30 to 33
#ASSERT NOT `Does the Act count what happened as the loss of my employment` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Q23. she was suspended
#ASSERT `Does the Act count what happened as the loss of my employment` FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Q23. nothing happened to her employment
#ASSERT NOT `Does the Act count what happened as the loss of my employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Q24. Ben left of his own choice (s 29(b.1))
#ASSERT `Does the Act count what I did as voluntarily leaving my employment` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Q24. he refused to resume the employment
#ASSERT `Does the Act count what I did as voluntarily leaving my employment` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Q24. he did not leave or refuse
#ASSERT NOT `Does the Act count what I did as voluntarily leaving my employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Q25. he refused work offered as an alternative to a lay-off; the lay-off happened on 29 May 2026 (s 29(b.1)(i))
#ASSERT `On what day does my refusal count as my voluntarily leaving` TRUE (YMD 2026 5 29) FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 7 1) (YMD 2026 5 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 5 29)
-- Q25. he refused to resume; he was supposed to resume on 1 June 2026 (s 29(b.1)(ii))
#ASSERT `On what day does my refusal count as my voluntarily leaving` FALSE (YMD 2026 5 29) TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 7 1) (YMD 2026 5 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 6 1)
-- Q25. he refused to continue after a transfer on 1 July 2026 (s 29(b.1)(iii))
#ASSERT `On what day does my refusal count as my voluntarily leaving` FALSE (YMD 2026 5 29) FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 7 1) (YMD 2026 5 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 7 1)
-- Q25. no refusal: the day he actually left, 1 May 2026
#ASSERT `On what day does my refusal count as my voluntarily leaving` FALSE (YMD 2026 5 29) FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 7 1) (YMD 2026 5 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 5 1)
-- Q26. Ben had no reasonable alternative to leaving (s 29(c))
#ASSERT `Did I have just cause for leaving or taking leave` TRUE
-- Q26. he had a reasonable alternative
#ASSERT NOT `Did I have just cause for leaving or taking leave` FALSE
-- Q27. Ben was harassed at work (s 29(c)(i))
#ASSERT `Is one of the circumstances the Act lists present` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Q27. a circumstance prescribed by regulation 51.1 applies (s 29(c)(xiv))
#ASSERT `Is one of the circumstances the Act lists present` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Q27. none of the listed circumstances
#ASSERT NOT `Is one of the circumstances the Act lists present` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Q28. Ana lost a job because of her misconduct; 100 of the 600 hours she needs since; not disentitled under ss 31 to 33 (s 30(1))
#ASSERT `Am I disqualified because I lost a job through misconduct or left without just cause` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 600 FALSE
-- Q28. since then she has had the 600 hours: s 30(1)(a)
#ASSERT NOT `Am I disqualified because I lost a job through misconduct or left without just cause` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 600 600 FALSE
-- Q28. 599 hours is not enough
#ASSERT `Am I disqualified because I lost a job through misconduct or left without just cause` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 599 600 FALSE
-- Q28. she is disentitled under ss 31 to 33 in relation to that job: s 30(1)(b)
#ASSERT NOT `Am I disqualified because I lost a job through misconduct or left without just cause` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 600 TRUE
-- Q28. Ben left without just cause; staying would not have cost his union rights
#ASSERT `Am I disqualified because I lost a job through misconduct or left without just cause` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 600 FALSE
-- Q28. Ben left without just cause only to keep his right to stay in his union (s 35)
#ASSERT NOT `Am I disqualified because I lost a job through misconduct or left without just cause` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 100 600 FALSE
-- Q28. the union exception needs his only reason to be the leaving
#ASSERT `Am I disqualified because I lost a job through misconduct or left without just cause` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 600 FALSE
-- Q29. Ana is disqualified; the week of Sunday 11 January 2026 follows her one-week waiting period (4 to 10 January) in a benefit period of 4 January to 26 December 2026 (s 30(2))
#ASSERT `Is this week one for which I am disqualified under section 30` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 11) (YMD 2026 1 4) (YMD 2026 12 26) (YMD 2026 1 4) (YMD 2026 1 10) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`
-- Q29. the week of Sunday 4 January 2026 is the waiting period
#ASSERT NOT `Is this week one for which I am disqualified under section 30` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 4) (YMD 2026 1 4) (YMD 2026 12 26) (YMD 2026 1 4) (YMD 2026 1 10) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`
-- Q29. she is otherwise entitled to special benefits that week: the disqualification is suspended (s 30(4))
#ASSERT NOT `Is this week one for which I am disqualified under section 30` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 11) (YMD 2026 1 4) (YMD 2026 12 26) (YMD 2026 1 4) (YMD 2026 1 10) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE `pregnancy`
-- Q29. the event happened on Thursday 12 March 2026 within the benefit period: the week of Sunday 1 March is before it (s 30(3))
#ASSERT NOT `Is this week one for which I am disqualified under section 30` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 1 4) (YMD 2026 12 26) (YMD 2026 1 4) (YMD 2026 1 10) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 12) FALSE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`
-- Q29. the week of Sunday 8 March 2026 is the week of the event
#ASSERT `Is this week one for which I am disqualified under section 30` TRUE (YMD 2026 3 8) (YMD 2026 1 4) (YMD 2026 12 26) (YMD 2026 1 4) (YMD 2026 1 10) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 12) FALSE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`
-- Q29. she is not disqualified under s 30(1)
#ASSERT NOT `Is this week one for which I am disqualified under section 30` FALSE (YMD 2026 1 11) (YMD 2026 1 4) (YMD 2026 12 26) (YMD 2026 1 4) (YMD 2026 1 10) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`
-- Q30. Ana had 400 hours before the job she lost, 200 in a later job she also lost, and 300 in jobs she did not lose: 300 may be used to qualify (s 30(5))
#ASSERT `How many hours can I use to qualify after losing or leaving a job` 400 200 300 EQUALS 300
-- Q30. all her hours were in jobs she did not lose or leave
#ASSERT `How many hours can I use to qualify after losing or leaving a job` 0 0 500 EQUALS 500
-- Q31. 300 hours in jobs she lost or left, 250 in others: 250 count for her maximum weeks and rate (s 30(6))
#ASSERT `How many hours can be used for my maximum weeks and my rate` 300 250 EQUALS 250
-- Q32. Cy is suspended for misconduct and nothing has ended it (s 31)
#ASSERT `Am I not entitled to benefits because I am suspended for misconduct` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 600
-- Q32. the suspension has expired
#ASSERT NOT `Am I not entitled to benefits because I am suspended for misconduct` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 600
-- Q32. he has lost or left the job
#ASSERT NOT `Am I not entitled to benefits because I am suspended for misconduct` TRUE FALSE TRUE 0 600
-- Q32. he has accumulated 600 hours with another employer
#ASSERT NOT `Am I not entitled to benefits because I am suspended for misconduct` TRUE FALSE FALSE 600 600
-- Q32. 599 hours is not enough
#ASSERT `Am I not entitled to benefits because I am suspended for misconduct` TRUE FALSE FALSE 599 600
-- Q32. he is not suspended for misconduct
#ASSERT NOT `Am I not entitled to benefits because I am suspended for misconduct` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 600
-- Q33. Di took leave without just cause, authorized by her employer, with an agreed return day (s 32(1))
#ASSERT `Am I not entitled to benefits because I took leave without just cause` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Q33. the employer did not authorize the leave
#ASSERT NOT `Am I not entitled to benefits because I took leave without just cause` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Q34. Di has resumed the employment: the disentitlement has ended (s 32(2)(a))
#ASSERT `Has my disentitlement for taking leave ended` TRUE FALSE 0 600
-- Q34. she has not resumed, left, or accumulated 600 hours
#ASSERT NOT `Has my disentitlement for taking leave ended` FALSE FALSE 599 600
-- Q34. she has accumulated 600 hours with another employer (s 32(2)(c))
#ASSERT `Has my disentitlement for taking leave ended` FALSE FALSE 600 600
-- Q35. Ed was dismissed for misconduct on 1 June 2026, 21 days before his set term expires on 22 June 2026 (s 33(1))
#ASSERT `Am I not entitled to benefits because I lost or left a job just before its end` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 6 22) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1)
-- Q35. he was dismissed on 31 May 2026, 22 days before
#ASSERT NOT `Am I not entitled to benefits because I lost or left a job just before its end` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 5 31) TRUE (YMD 2026 6 22) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1)
-- Q35. Fay left without just cause on 20 June 2026, having been told she would be laid off on 30 June 2026
#ASSERT `Am I not entitled to benefits because I lost or left a job just before its end` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 20) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 6 30)
-- Q35. Fay left only to keep her right to follow her union's rules (s 35)
#ASSERT NOT `Am I not entitled to benefits because I lost or left a job just before its end` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 20) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 6 30)
-- Q35. no set term and no notice of a lay-off
#ASSERT NOT `Am I not entitled to benefits because I lost or left a job just before its end` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 20) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1)
-- Q36. Ed's disentitlement lasts until the term expires: still in force on 22 June 2026 (s 33(2))
#ASSERT `Is my disentitlement for an anticipated loss still in force on this day` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 22) (YMD 2026 6 22)
-- Q36. not in force on 23 June 2026
#ASSERT NOT `Is my disentitlement for an anticipated loss still in force on this day` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 23) (YMD 2026 6 22)
-- Q36. he is not under s 33(1)
#ASSERT NOT `Is my disentitlement for an anticipated loss still in force on this day` FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 22)
-- Q37. Ed is disentitled and otherwise entitled to compassionate care benefits for the week: special benefits, so suspended (s 34)
#ASSERT `Is my disentitlement suspended for this week` TRUE TRUE `care or support of a family member`
-- Q37. he is otherwise entitled only to regular benefits
#ASSERT NOT `Is my disentitlement suspended for this week` TRUE TRUE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`
-- Q37. not otherwise entitled to any benefits
#ASSERT NOT `Is my disentitlement suspended for this week` TRUE FALSE `care or support of a family member`
-- Q38. Fay's only reason is that she left, and staying would have cost her union rights (s 35)
